{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"a677884d447e0046951c5c25e5f738405a38b2150025da7570732a8c5f94785a","digest":{"component_or_area":"Operation certificates (plan-review and completion-verifier attestation)","key_entities":["rebar.opcert.v1",".rebar/trusted_environments.yaml","src/rebar/attest/registry.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py",".opcert-key",".github/workflows/verify-identity.yaml","src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","src/rebar/attest/hmac_legacy.py","docs/adr/0046-security-posture-and-accepted-limitations.md","docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md","verify.require_environment","verify.opcert_enforce_since","verify.opcert_remote_url","added_at_commit","revoked_at_commit","key_not_valid_at_era","SIGNATURE event","material_fingerprint","merged_log_commit"],"problem_keywords":["operation certificates","asymmetric signatures","environment attribution","op-cert verification","trusted environment","HMAC removal","key rotation","merge-gate enforcement","authoritative-state fetch","high-assurance projects"],"propositions":["Operation certificates are today self-signed with symmetric HMAC secrets per clone, unverifiable by third parties, and provide no enforceable control; they must migrate to asymmetric Ed25519 signatures minted by environments and verifiable against pinned public keys.","Projects have no way to require that a gate verdict (plan-review or completion-verifier) came from a specific trusted environment; they need optional per-project required-environment policy enforced at the merge gate with out-of-band key pinning in .rebar/trusted_environments.yaml.","The legacy HMAC scheme must be removed once op-certs sign asymmetrically, completing the migration; both operation-cert and authorship signatures must be asymmetric, with a named expand-contract migration artifact documenting the cutover procedure.","A trusted remote environment that signs operation certificates must fetch authoritative ticket state and code from primary sources itself, never use client-supplied inputs, to ensure the certificate attests to verified facts; this requires a stateless remote service with IAM-authenticated access.","Environment-key rotation must be era-scoped using commit-ancestry validity evaluated at the certificate's storage anchor (the SIGNATURE event's introducing commit on the tickets branch), not at the certificate's self-chosen merged-log-commit, to prevent rollback attacks on revoked keys.","The default local path must remain offline, never require network access, and never wedge an operation; high-security required-environment policy and trusted remote execution are opt-in and do not become mandatory."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785820546066803926,"uuid":"f67ad2eb-998f-4c4b-b31f-79d9729faf76"}